  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 10 actions (actions.js, single setActionDefinitions call) and 1 advanced feedback (feedbacks.js). Nothing is generated at runtime except the choice lists of source and preset.",
    "Protocol: the module talks to the device through the npm package @novastar-dev/coex (its transport was not read, not part of the clone) with config fields host (Regex.IP) and port (Regex.PORT, default 8001). Manifest description: COEX/VMP devices (MX40 Pro, MX30, CX80 Pro).",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ^1.11.3 (1.x): options do not support expressions. Module version in package.json is 2.0.2; manifest.json carries the placeholder version 0.0.0.",
    "display_mode uses numeric ids 0/1/2 and set_3dlut_status uses boolean ids true/false; the source keeps these types (the booleans are not strings).",
    "Brightness and gamma calls pass screenId null (all screens); the screenids field of set_3dlut_status is trimmed and blank means all screens.",
    "The testpattern action always sends the red/green/blue/gray/gridWidth/moveSpeed/gradientStretch values together with state 1 whatever the chosen pattern; the static-text option id params carries no value.",
    "The toggle actions read the display mode of the first screen only (displayState[0].displayMode); toggle_blackout switches Freeze and unknown to Blackout, toggle_freeze switches Blackout and unknown to Freeze.",
    "Variables (variables.js) and the upgrade scripts (empty) are not catalogued; the module has no presets file."
  ]
